{"Test does not prove denial cache overrides an allowed permission cache - the permission cache is set with false as the map value, so checkPermission would also deny the request on its own, meaning the denial cache is never proven to be the reason for the false outcome. The map value should be true to properly verify denial cache priority.": 0.906812846660614, "Denial cache keyed on unresolved UID (raw string from gRPC subject like '12345') while permission cache uses resolved UID from GetUserIdentifiers (like 'abc-def-123'), causing inconsistency where users can be wrongly denied after permissions are granted if requested with different UID formats within the TTL.": 0.39482492208480835, "Cache hit reported as miss when cached permissions do not cover the requested resource - when getCachedIdentityPermissions succeeds but checkPermission returns allowed=false, the metric records permissionCacheUsage('false') even though the permission cache was successfully read, understating cache effectiveness.": 0.7947414517402649, "Potential key collision in denial cache due to undelimited concatenation - using underscore as separator means different (name, parent) pairs can produce the same key if components contain underscores (e.g., name='dash_1', parent='' collides with name='dash', parent='1_').": 0.6183862090110779}